From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: boozedog <code@booze.dog>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:13:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: gs201-felix: enable the GPU

The Pixel Fold's Mali-G710 is the same gs201 GPU as the Pixel 7 Pro.
There is no mali-supply: the G3D rails follow the PMU power domain and
ACPM.

On 7.3.0-rc6-omandroid-push1-gb60e882f0c1f (built 2026-10-17) Panthor
1.9.0 bound at 151 MHz. Mali-G710 id 0xa862, shader_present=0x1110055.
CSF firmware 95a25d71030715381f33105394285e1dcc860a65, interface
v1.5.0. Probe reported no mali regulator, which matches this node.

glmark2-es2-drm scanned out through the cover simple-framebuffer
(1080x2092). The renderer was Mali-G710 MC7 (Panfrost), OpenGL ES 3.1,
Mesa 26.2.4-arch1.1.3.omamobile3. One vsynced scene
scored 51. No GPU fault.

Signed-off-by: boozedog <code@booze.dog>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-felix.dts | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-felix.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-felix.dts
index 19275f2b2..3dd715dac 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-felix.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-felix.dts
@@ -3,8 +3,8 @@
  * Google Pixel Fold (felix).
  *
  * Same GS201 silicon as the Pixel 7 Pro. This board file brings up USB,
- * the cover framebuffer the bootloader is already scanning, and UFS.
- * It does not describe either panel or either touch controller. The
+ * the cover framebuffer the bootloader is already scanning, UFS, and the
+ * GPU. It does not describe either panel or either touch controller. The
  * inner panel has no node that could drive it.
  */
 
@@ -90,3 +90,8 @@ &ufs_0 {
 &ufs_0_phy {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+&gpu {
+	/* No mali-supply: the G3D rails follow the PMU power domain and ACPM. */
+	status = "okay";
+};
